{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cfc5BKZD2E16rMDDvpcqv", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": ""}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7754, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16830, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7754}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "4f8ef44e-1eee-461b-8885-17bf35190411", "uuid": "d5c32dbb-00b3-4a6f-8891-3d6b4d6c29d2", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T19:31:01.087Z", "request_id": "req_011Cfc5BKJpje51GyNhRuhYY"}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cfc5BKZD2E16rMDDvpcqv", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**Banker's rounding** (also called round-half-to-even, or `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) changes only how exact ties are rounded. A value that falls exactly halfway between two choices goes to whichever neighbor is **even**. Everything else rounds normally.\n\n| Value | Round-half-up | Banker's (half-even) |\n|-------|---------------|----------------------|\n| 0.5   | 1             | **0**                |\n| 1.5   | 2             | 2                    |\n| 2.5   | 3             | **2**                |\n| 3.5   | 4             | 4                    |\n| 2.51  | 3             | 3 (not a tie)        |\n\nFor currency, apply the same rule at the cent: $1.245 \u2192 $1.24 and $1.255 \u2192 $1.26.\n\n### Why accountants like it\n\n1. **No upward drift.** With round-half-up, every tie goes up, so across thousands of line items the totals slowly inflate. Banker's rounding sends about half the ties up and half down, so on average the rounding errors cancel out. Sums of rounded values stay close to the rounded sum of the true values.\n\n2. **Totals reconcile better.** Ledgers, invoices and tax reports often compare a sum of rounded items with a rounded total. Less bias means fewer off-by-a-cent differences to explain or write off.\n\n3. **It's fair to both sides.** In interest, tax or currency conversion, consistently rounding ties up favors one party. Half-even is neutral.\n\n4. **It's an established standard.** It is the default rounding mode in IEEE 754 floating point, and Python's `decimal` module and built-in `round()` both use it. Many financial systems and some regulations either specify it or accept it.\n\n### Caveats\n\n- It only matters for **exact ties**, so you need exact decimal arithmetic (for example, Python's `Decimal`, not binary floats). With floats, `2.675` is really stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so it never reaches the tie-breaking rule.\n- Some jurisdictions or contracts require round-half-up for specific calculations, so check the governing rule before choosing.\n\nThis applies to this repo too: a stored project decision says tax amounts use `decimal.ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, agreed with the finance team in March 2026, and that `ROUND_HALF_UP` shouldn't be used."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7754, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16830, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7754}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "4f8ef44e-1eee-461b-8885-17bf35190411", "uuid": "f52e66c4-b7f8-48c4-a768-787b68930d55", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T19:31:08.767Z", "request_id": "req_011Cfc5BKJpje51GyNhRuhYY"}
